    id: 'narad', name: 'Narad', type: 'engine',
    oneLiner: 'Connectivity and Infrastructure - the communication backbone connecting the ecosystem to all external systems.',
    summary: 'Narad is the connectivity layer managing all external communication between the Algo IQ Ecosystem and brokers, exchanges, data vendors, SEBI systems, and partner APIs. It handles network management, authentication, protocol translation, circuit switching, and connection monitoring.',
    points: [
      { title: 'Central Connectivity Hub', explanation: 'Narad acts as the single connectivity gateway for all external interactions. Every broker connection, exchange feed, API call, and data vendor subscription flows through Narad. This centralization simplifies security and provides a single observability point.' },
      { title: 'Broker Connection Management', explanation: 'Narad maintains persistent connections to 12+ broker systems including XTS, Greeksoft, Zerodha, Upstox, and institutional brokers. It handles broker-specific authentication, session keep-alive, and graceful reconnection on loss.' },
      { title: 'Protocol Translation', explanation: 'External systems use diverse protocols: FIX, REST, WebSocket, gRPC, and proprietary. Narad translates all incoming data into the ecosystem internal MQ message format. No other component needs to handle external protocols.' },
      { title: 'Circuit Switching and Failover', explanation: 'Narad implements automatic circuit switching between primary and backup connections. If a primary broker connection fails, Narad seamlessly switches to a backup route. The switch is transparent to upstream components.' },
      { title: 'Network Security', explanation: 'Narad enforces network-level security: TLS encryption for all external connections, IP whitelisting for incoming connections, VPN tunneling to broker networks, and mutual certificate authentication.' },
      { title: 'Rate Limiting and Throttling', explanation: 'Exchanges and brokers impose API rate limits. Narad enforces these limits by queuing requests and throttling as needed using token-bucket algorithms per connection to prevent rate limit violations.' },
      { title: 'Health Monitoring', explanation: 'Narad continuously monitors every external connection: latency, error rate, throughput, and uptime. Connection health metrics are published to Kavach for alerting and DXCC for operational visibility.' },
      { title: 'Leased Line Management', explanation: 'For low-latency exchange connectivity, Narad manages leased line connections to NSE and BSE colocation facilities. It monitors line quality, latency, and packet loss with automatic failover to backup connections.' },
      { title: 'Input from Internal Components', explanation: 'When Vega needs to send an order or Surya needs to download a file or Lakshmi needs a market feed - all these requests go through Narad. Internal components communicate intent via MQ; Narad handles the external leg.' },
      { title: 'Output to Internal Components', explanation: 'Responses from external systems - order confirmations, file downloads, market data - are received by Narad, translated into internal formats, and published to appropriate MQ topics for upstream consumers.' },
      { title: 'Business Value', explanation: 'Narad isolates the complexity of external connectivity from business logic. Engine developers do not need to understand broker protocols. Adding a new broker connection benefits the entire ecosystem without touching any engine.' },
      { title: 'Failure Impact', explanation: 'If Narad goes down, the ecosystem is completely cut off from the outside world. No orders reach brokers, no market data arrives, no exchange files are downloaded. Trading effectively stops. Full redundancy with auto-failover is required.' },
      { title: 'Session Persistence', explanation: 'Narad maintains session state across connection drops. If a broker session disconnects and reconnects, Narad restores session context so upstream components do not need to reinitialize.' },
      { title: 'Latency Optimization', explanation: 'For latency-sensitive connections, Narad uses non-blocking I/O and direct memory access. Market data and order routing connections bypass translation where possible using zero-copy message forwarding.' },
      { title: 'Dependency on Suraksha', explanation: 'Narad coordinates with Suraksha for security decisions. If Suraksha detects a compromised session or unauthorized access, it instructs Narad to terminate the connection immediately.' },
      { title: 'Logging for Audit', explanation: 'Every external communication through Narad is logged with full request/response details. These logs feed Chitragupta audit trail for compliance and troubleshooting with timestamps, endpoints, and status codes.' },
      { title: 'SEBI Compliance Connectivity', explanation: 'Narad handles connections to SEBI-mandated systems for compliance reporting, trade verification, and regulatory filings. These connections have strict uptime and security requirements.' },
      { title: 'VPN and Lease Line Management', explanation: 'Narad manages VPN tunnels and leased lines connecting Algo IQ data center to broker and exchange networks. It handles tunnel health monitoring, auto-reconnection, and secure key rotation.' },
      { title: 'Load Balancing', explanation: 'Narad distributes outgoing requests across multiple connections to the same broker when available. Load balancing increases throughput and provides resilience through automatic request shifting on failure.' },
      { title: 'Extensibility', explanation: 'Adding a new broker is a Narad configuration task. Pluggable architecture allows new connection handlers without modifying core Narad code. Protocol adapters, authentication handlers, and health checks are all modular.' },
    ],
